    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d954">

                <pb facs="0747" n="665" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg665"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.00/1645.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Chargé
                        d’Affaires.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-06-27"><hi rendition="#italic">June 27,
                        1911</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 28.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith a copy of the
                    Department’s letter of the 20th instant,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d954-f1"/> and a
                    copy of one dated the 21st instant from the Navy Department in reply
                        thereto,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d954-f2"/> from which you will observe that
                    the Navy Department has arranged for the <hi rendition="#italic">Yorktown</hi>
                    to remain at Corinto until relieved by the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Vicksburg</hi> and for the <hi rendition="#italic">Marietta</hi> to be kept
                    in wireless communication with Bluefields.</p>
                <p>You will communicate this information to the consuls at Corinto and
                    Bluefields.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
